<title>JAPAN: Japan March large store sales up 14.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan March large store sales up 14.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at Japanese department stores and supermarkets rose 14.1 percent in March from a year earlier to 2.27 trillion yen, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Monday.</p>
<p>MITI attributed the increase mainly to purchases of clothing due to the change in seasons and &quot;rush in&quot; demand before the consumption tax increase from April 1.</p>
<p>For the fiscal year ended March 1997, sales at Japanese department stores and supermarkets fell 0.4 percent from the previous year to 22.98 trillion yen, the ministry said.</p>
<p>The breakdown for the figures is as follows:</p>
<p>				  MAR	 FEB</p>
<p>    Overall change	+14.1	-1.9</p>
<p>	Dept stores	 +21.1	-0.1</p>
<p>	Supermarkets	+ 7.2	-3.4</p>
</text>
